\ thermostat.8th -- Thinking 8th, Chapter 3
\ Verified with: 8th code/ch03/thermostat.8th
\
\ A small component-based design: a mode-decision component (with one
\ hidden primitive, set-mode, shared by both the automatic and the
\ manual paths), and a sensor component with a forward-referenced
\ diagnostics hook, wired up only after the fact.

0 constant IDLE
1 constant HEATING
2 constant COOLING

IDLE var, mode

[ "idle" , "heating" , "cooling" ] constant mode-names

: mode@      \ -- mode
  mode @ ;

: mode-name  \ mode -- s
  mode-names swap caseof ;

\ The one place that knows both the old and the new mode -- and so the
\ one place that can decide, cheaply, whether anything actually changed.
: set-mode   \ new-mode --
  dup mode@ n:= not if
    dup mode !
    mode-name "now %s\n" s:strfmt .
  else
    drop
  then ;

\ Both the automatic decision below AND these manual overrides funnel
\ through set-mode -- that's what makes the change-detection above
\ apply uniformly, with no caller needing to know it's there.
: heat        HEATING set-mode ;
: cool        COOLING set-mode ;
: hvac-idle   IDLE    set-mode ;

: decide-mode  \ degrees -- new-mode
  dup 68 n:< if
    drop HEATING
  else
    76 n:> if COOLING else IDLE then
  then ;

\ --- sensor component ---

defer: on-bad-reading   \ degrees -- ; forward reference: filled in
                        \ below by a diagnostics component that doesn't
                        \ exist yet when read-temp is written.

: plausible?  \ degrees -- flag
  dup -20 n:> swap 120 n:< and ;

0 var, sensor-temp    \ stands in for a real sensor; easy to drive from tests

: read-temp  \ -- degrees
  sensor-temp @
  dup plausible? not if dup on-bad-reading then ;

: auto-cycle   \ --
  read-temp decide-mode set-mode ;

\ --- exercise the base design ---

60 sensor-temp !  auto-cycle    \ idle -> heating: logs
61 sensor-temp !  auto-cycle    \ still heating: silent
72 sensor-temp !  auto-cycle    \ heating -> idle: logs
999 sensor-temp ! auto-cycle    \ implausible AND idle -> cooling:
                                 \ mode-change logs; diagnostic hook is
                                 \ still a no-op, so it stays silent

\ --- the diagnostics component, designed and wired in afterward ---

: report-bad-reading  \ degrees --
  "sensor reading %d looks implausible -- check wiring\n" s:strfmt . ;

' report-bad-reading w:is on-bad-reading

999 sensor-temp ! auto-cycle    \ same bad reading, same mode (cooling):
                                 \ no mode-change log, but now diagnosed

mode@ mode-name "final mode: %s\n" s:strfmt .

bye
